      {
        "id": "u1",
        "kind": "CONCEPT",
        "label": "Definition of redox as electron transfer",
        "attributes": {
          "depth": "explanation"
        },
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s1"
        ],
        "rationale": "Introduces redox reactions by explaining them as electron transfer processes and drawing parallels to acid-base proton transfer.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
          "value": "none",
          "evidence": []
        },
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p1",
            "category": "ANALOGY",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Bonjour ! Installe-toi. Ne t'inquiète pas : les réactions d'oxydoréduction (qu'on appelle souvent **« redox »**), ça a l'air barbare comme nom, mais c'est en réalité **un simple échange de cadeaux**. ",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 200
          },
          {
            "id": "p2",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Sauf qu'en chimie, les cadeaux sont des **électrons ($e^-$)**.",
            "start": 202,
            "end": 264
          },
          {
            "id": "p3",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Tu as déjà vu les réactions acido-basiques où les molécules s'échangent des protons ($H^+$) ? Eh bien la redox, c'est exactement la même idée, mais avec des **électrons ($e^-$)**.",
            "start": 266,
            "end": 445
          },
          {
            "id": "p4",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Voici le guide complet pour tout comprendre et réussir tes devoirs.",
            "start": 447,
            "end": 514
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "Correctly defines redox reactions as involving electron transfer, accurately drawing an analogy with the proton-transfer model of acid-base reactions.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
