            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "### 3. Un exemple concret : Le clou de zinc et l'eau bleue",
            "start": 1814,
            "end": 1872
          },
          {
            "id": "p26",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Imaginons qu'on plonge une plaque de Zinc ($\\text{Zn}$) dans une solution bleue contenant des ions Cuivre ($\\text{Cu}^{2+}$). Que se passe-t-il ?",
            "start": 1874,
            "end": 2019
          },
          {
            "id": "p27",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "On a deux couples en présence : $\\text{Cu}^{2+} / \\text{Cu}$ et $\\text{Zn}^{2+} / \\text{Zn}$.",
            "start": 2021,
            "end": 2114
          },
          {
            "id": "p28",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "1.  **Le Cuivre ($\\text{Cu}^{2+}$)** est un oxydant, il veut des électrons :",
            "start": 2116,
            "end": 2192
          },
          {
            "id": "p29",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "equation"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "    $$\\text{Cu}^{2+} + 2e^- \\rightarrow \\text{Cu} \\quad \\text{(C'est une Réduction)}$$",
            "start": 2193,
            "end": 2279
          },
          {
            "id": "p30",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "2.  **Le Zinc ($\\text{Zn}$)** est un réducteur, il donne ses électrons :",
            "start": 2280,
            "end": 2352
          },
          {
            "id": "p31",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "equation"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "    $$\\text{Zn} \\rightarrow \\text{Zn}^{2+} + 2e^- \\quad \\text{(C'est une Oxydation)}$$",
            "start": 2353,
            "end": 2439
          },
          {
            "id": "p32",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "**L'équation bilan :**",
            "start": 2441,
            "end": 2463
          },
          {
            "id": "p33",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Les électrons ne se promènent jamais tout seuls dans la nature. Le Zinc donne ses 2 électrons directement au Cuivre. On additionne les deux demi-équations :",
            "start": 2464,
            "end": 2620
          },
          {
            "id": "p34",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "equation"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "$$\\text{Cu}^{2+} + \\text{Zn} \\rightarrow \\text{Cu} + \\text{Zn}^{2+}$$",
            "start": 2622,
            "end": 2691
          },
          {
            "id": "p35",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "*Résultat dans le bécher :* La solution perd sa couleur bleue (les $\\text{Cu}^{2+}$ disparaissent) et un dépôt de cuivre métallique rouge/marron ($\\text{Cu}$) apparaît sur la plaque !",
            "start": 2693,
            "end": 2876
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "All equations (Cu2+ reduction, Zn oxidation, and overall reaction) and the physical observations (discoloration of the blue solution, reddish-brown copper deposit) are chemically accurate.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
